HSRP – First Hop Redundancy Lab

Objective: Demonstrate gateway redundancy using Cisco Hot Standby Router Protocol (HSRP).

Network Configuration:

GW1 Physical IP: 192.168.1.1

GW2 Physical IP: 192.168.1.2

HSRP Virtual IP: 192.168.1.3

HSRP Group: 1

PC IP Range: 192.168.1.10 – 192.168.1.40

Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.0

Loopback Test IP: 8.8.8.8

Important Instructions:

Both routers are configured for HSRP Group 1.

All PCs must use 192.168.1.3 as their default gateway.

GW1 and GW2 provide Active/Standby gateway redundancy.

Shut down the Active router's FastEthernet0/0 interface to simulate failure.

Verify that the Standby router takes over the Active role.

Test connectivity again without changing the PCs' default gateway.

Learning Outcome:

Understand HSRP operation, virtual IP addressing, Active/Standby router roles, gateway redundancy and failover behaviour.

Refer to README.txt for complete configuration instructions and troubleshooting.
